    "final_answer": "Upgraded `payout_sync.py` to the v2 export API.\n\n### Changes\n- Switched from `GET /v1/payouts` to `GET /v2/payouts`.\n- Follows the opaque `cursor` until `drained: true`.\n- Deduplicates by payout `id`, since v2 windows overlap at their boundaries.\n- Retries `429` responses using `Retry-After`, replaying the identical request.\n- Restarts the export from the beginning on an `invalid_cursor` `400`.\n- Keeps the existing CLI and output format unchanged.\n\n### Verification against the v2 server\nRan the updated consumer against `http://the VM's public address:18080` and the grading instance:\n\n- Synced **2431** payouts\n- **2431** unique IDs\n- First `po_00001`, last `po_02431`\n- Output was byte-identical to the v1 baseline\n- Verified cursor paging with small windows matched the full result\n- Verified 429 handling: the server throttled 4 traversals, and each was retried successfully with the exact same request\n- Verified invalid-cursor recovery restarts cleanly and still returns the complete set",
